[
  // Manufacturing components: Leatherworking, Tailoring, Fletching and Artifice all stop one
  // step short of finished gear and hand a *part* to the fabrication system.
  //
  // The leathers are per-creature on purpose (docs/professions.md §12). A single tiered
  // "Leather 1/2/3" would throw away the only interesting thing about a hide — drake leather
  // is worth curing because it keeps its heat resistance, not because it is a bigger number.
  //
  // Note the double `form:` tags. A processed part is still made of what it was made of: cured
  // leather is hide, woven cloth is fibre, a shaped stave is wood. Carrying both the source
  // form and the worked form is what makes these legal in the fabrication slots that ask for
  // `form:hide` / `form:fiber` / `form:wood` — a bow stave really is a usable sword grip.

